  <h1>The JobFoundry Manifesto</h1>
  <p><em>Why this tool exists, and who it is for.</em></p>

  <h2>1. Job hunting is hard enough. The tooling should not make it harder.</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>JobFoundry meets people where they already are: the browser.</strong> If you
    can browse job sites, you can use JobFoundry. No AI coding assistant, no terminal, no
    prompt skills. Install the app, add the extension, keep browsing like always — capture,
    dedup, scoring, tailoring, and tracking happen quietly, locally, under your control.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Your career data belongs to you. Entirely.</h2>
  <p>
    Your resume is your life on paper. JobFoundry stores everything on your machine, phones
    home to nobody, and works offline except for the LLM provider <em>you</em> choose.
    Local-first is not a feature here. It is the premise.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Reading a public job posting should never cost an LLM call.</h2>
  <p>
    Our zero-token philosophy: structured data comes from public ATS endpoints, feeds, and
    markup — free, fast, private. Models are spent only where judgment is needed: scoring
    fit and tailoring resumes. No AI subscription required to discover jobs.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Scrape from where the jobs are visible: the browser.</h2>
  <p>
    Server scrapers lose to Cloudflare, CAPTCHAs, and login walls daily. Your browser
    session walks straight through — so capture happens in your browser and the server
    never touches a job board. A reliability decision first, a privacy decision second.
  </p>

  <h2>5. A tailored resume must be true.</h2>
  <p>
    Tools that invent employers and skills set candidates up to fail background checks.
    JobFoundry re-ranks and rephrases <em>your genuine experience</em> under strict schema
    constraints, with protected fields that never change. Truth over fabrication, always.
  </p>

  <h2>6. The human applies. The tool prepares.</h2>
  <p>
    JobFoundry evaluates, drafts, organizes, and reminds. It never auto-submits, never
    spams employers. Fewer, better, honest applications beat spray-and-pray.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Free software, forever.</h2>
  <p>
    AGPL-3.0. Inspect every line, self-host, fork, and leave with your data anytime. Tools
    for vulnerable moments in people's lives must not become traps.
  </p>

  <p>
    The canonical version lives in
    <a href="https://github.com/deadrat-in/JobFoundry/blob/main/MANIFESTO.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><code>MANIFESTO.md</code></a>.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
